WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:05.403 --> 00:00:07.782
<i>In Toronto's
war on crime.</i>

2
00:00:07.783 --> 00:00:10.092
<i>the worst offenders
are pursued by the detectives</i>

3
00:00:10.093 --> 00:00:12.989
<i>of the Specialized
Criminal Investigations Unit.</i>

4
00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.299
<i>These are their stories.</i>

5
00:00:17.921 --> 00:00:20.782
The arctic is crawling
with polar bears.

6
00:00:20.783 --> 00:00:22.816
and they're hungry.
and Logan the Brave.

7
00:00:22.817 --> 00:00:25.161
a six year old explorer--
- Six and a half.

8
00:00:25.162 --> 00:00:27.299
Swings across
to the other side.

9
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.747
Unless he'd rather his dad
show him how it's done.

10
00:00:29.748 --> 00:00:32.782
Oh. one's got his leg!

11
00:00:32.783 --> 00:00:34.058
Take that polar bear!

12
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.540
You really think you could
do the monkey bars?

13
00:00:40.541 --> 00:00:42.196
Not a chance.

14
00:00:44.955 --> 00:00:46.747
Drinking
on the job. huh?

15
00:00:49.231 --> 00:00:51.747
I was. Your husband
wasn't having any.

16
00:00:51.748 --> 00:00:55.162
It's funny. that. uh. your
flask has his initials on it.

17
00:00:56.817 --> 00:00:58.714
I'll get the car.

18
00:01:02.679 --> 00:01:03.782
Come on. bud. let's go.

19
00:01:03.783 --> 00:01:05.368
Not yet.

20
00:01:05.369 --> 00:01:09.885
Logan. Right now.
Hey! Come back here right now.

21
00:01:09.886 --> 00:01:12.954
Logan. get down from there.
I mean it.

22
00:01:12.955 --> 00:01:14.885
Right now!

23
00:01:14.886 --> 00:01:16.852
My arm!

24
00:01:19.714 --> 00:01:21.299
- Come on. come on.
- What happened?

25
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.713
- Nell. it's fine.
- Logan!

26
00:01:22.714 --> 00:01:24.195
- We're fine!
- Logan!

27
00:01:24.196 --> 00:01:25.747
Can you get up?

28
00:01:25.748 --> 00:01:28.368
Just give him a little bit
of space. give him space.

29
00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:29.851
Hey you okay? What happened?

30
00:01:29.852 --> 00:01:31.506
So between Logan's testimony

31
00:01:31.507 --> 00:01:33.195
and the eye witnesses.
this case is cut and dry.

32
00:01:33.196 --> 00:01:35.540
but. never hurts to hear
from a grandparent.

33
00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:37.506
Grandparents are old.
I go by papa.

34
00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.610
Sorry. My new intern
is a nepotism hire.

35
00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:47.231
Marcy. just push the button.
The red button.

36
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:55.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

37
00:02:07.196 --> 00:02:09.196
Oh. Nell.

38
00:02:33.162 --> 00:02:34.403
Hey.

39
00:02:35.472 --> 00:02:36.678
Can I help you?

40
00:02:36.679 --> 00:02:39.402
Yeah. actually.
I'm looking for a rug.

41
00:02:39.403 --> 00:02:42.333
Something that doesnt stain.

42
00:02:55.024 --> 00:02:56.816
Yes!

43
00:02:56.817 --> 00:02:59.368
Applaud for yourselves.

44
00:02:59.369 --> 00:03:04.540
So. grab an ass and light some
grass as we prepare to screen

45
00:03:04.541 --> 00:03:06.713
our first film.

46
00:03:08.817 --> 00:03:12.817
And who is
the first victim it is.

47
00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:19.368
Who's responsible
for this masterpiece?

48
00:03:19.369 --> 00:03:22.161
Anyone? No?

49
00:03:22.162 --> 00:03:23.679
Our first director is shy.

50
00:03:26.403 --> 00:03:28.852
And... lights.

51
00:03:34.438 --> 00:03:39.402
<i>No. help! Help!
Somebody help! Somebody please
help me!</i>

52
00:04:34.093 --> 00:04:38.126
Shut it off!

53
00:05:19.438 --> 00:05:21.678
What is this place?

54
00:05:21.679 --> 00:05:23.506
You've never been
to the cinefile?

55
00:05:23.507 --> 00:05:27.472
Uh. no. But. uh. can't say
I'm surprised that you have.

56
00:05:29.369 --> 00:05:31.300
Henry.

57
00:05:33.714 --> 00:05:35.747
And you must be
detective Bateman.

58
00:05:35.748 --> 00:05:37.437
Yeah.

59
00:05:37.438 --> 00:05:38.851
Ah. oh.

60
00:05:38.852 --> 00:05:40.885
Welcome to Cinephile.

61
00:05:40.886 --> 00:05:45.092
Toronto's premiere showcase
for the weird and the wicked.

62
00:05:45.093 --> 00:05:48.507
And we now have a brand new
claim to fame.

63
00:05:52.472 --> 00:05:54.990
Murder.

64
00:05:57.231 --> 00:06:01.644
I didn't drag you down here
for some AI slop.

65
00:06:01.645 --> 00:06:05.057
This is a genuine snuff film.

66
00:06:05.058 --> 00:06:08.920
<i>No. no.
no. please. don't!</i>

67
00:06:17.645 --> 00:06:19.989
Well. the aberrations
of the camera lens

68
00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.161
reads like an older model.
high 8 maybe?

69
00:06:22.162 --> 00:06:25.023
Shh. shh. This guy's not dead.

70
00:06:25.024 --> 00:06:29.126
Not yet. anyway. It's a minor
concussion at best.

71
00:06:32.507 --> 00:06:36.644
All right. Look at the way
it bubbles around

72
00:06:36.645 --> 00:06:41.299
the quickly viscous quality
of the skin. That is not CG.

73
00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.333
Darkening. coagulated.
that is the reaction

74
00:06:44.334 --> 00:06:47.714
of skin to exposure
to hydrochloric acid.

75
00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:52.092
Queasy feeling
you get from watching it.

76
00:06:52.093 --> 00:06:53.471
that's hard to fake.

77
00:06:53.472 --> 00:06:55.264
Shivers that run up your spine
when you realize

78
00:06:55.265 --> 00:06:59.126
you've just witnessed someone
perishing before your very eyes.

79
00:06:59.127 --> 00:07:00.713
Should we have another go?

80
00:07:00.714 --> 00:07:04.230
No. uh. less is more.
Less.

81
00:07:04.231 --> 00:07:08.092
This was a RSVP event?
- Of course.

82
00:07:08.093 --> 00:07:10.402
We're gonna need to get the
names of everyone in attendance.

83
00:07:10.403 --> 00:07:13.644
Sure. but everyone here
was at a wrap party

84
00:07:13.645 --> 00:07:15.057
when that DVD was delivered.

85
00:07:15.058 --> 00:07:16.609
How do you know when that was?

86
00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:19.402
Because. like almost
everything great in life.

87
00:07:19.403 --> 00:07:22.575
it was captured on film.

88
00:07:22.576 --> 00:07:25.954
This was captured
on Cinephile's doorbell cam.

89
00:07:25.955 --> 00:07:27.782
Two nights ago someone
dropped the DVD

90
00:07:27.783 --> 00:07:30.471
in the festival's submission
box at 7 05 P.M..

91
00:07:30.472 --> 00:07:32.782
same time as Les
and the other participants

92
00:07:32.783 --> 00:07:35.437
were at the Spaghetti Factory
for the wrap party.

93
00:07:35.438 --> 00:07:37.885
Yeah. we spoke to everyone
in attendance. but it appears

94
00:07:37.886 --> 00:07:40.540
nobody has any connection
to the film whatsoever.

95
00:07:40.541 --> 00:07:42.506
So if no one at the Cinephile
was involved.

96
00:07:42.507 --> 00:07:44.230
why release the film there?

97
00:07:44.231 --> 00:07:46.092
No. we believe the Cinephile
was just a vehicle

98
00:07:46.093 --> 00:07:47.678
for getting the film
out to the world.

99
00:07:47.679 --> 00:07:49.747
Exactly. If the killer
had posted the video online.

100
00:07:49.748 --> 00:07:51.678
Mark would've already
had tracked him down.

101
00:07:51.679 --> 00:07:53.954
So how do you leak something
without leaving a trace?

102
00:07:53.955 --> 00:07:55.540
Get somebody else
to do it for you.

103
00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:57.126
At the screening
one of the kids recorded

104
00:07:57.127 --> 00:08:00.195
the video on their phone
and posted it online.

105
00:08:00.196 --> 00:08:02.713
9.200 views and counting.

106
00:08:02.714 --> 00:08:05.299
And Les plastered
the entire city with posters

107
00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.954
for the screening. I mean.
the killer could be anyone.

108
00:08:07.955 --> 00:08:12.747
As could our victim. We cross
referenced this image against

109
00:08:12.748 --> 00:08:15.678
our missing persons registry.
So far no hits.

110
00:08:15.679 --> 00:08:17.437
Until we know that
this film is real.

111
00:08:17.438 --> 00:08:19.575
we don't even know
that this is Toronto.

112
00:08:19.576 --> 00:08:21.954
Yeah. but if the film is real.

113
00:08:21.955 --> 00:08:24.540
that liquid
is hydrochloric acid.

114
00:08:24.541 --> 00:08:27.816
which dissolves all traces
of DNA within 72 hours.

115
00:08:27.817 --> 00:08:29.609
Then we're running out
of time.

116
00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:31.195
Our victim
is a white male.

117
00:08:31.196 --> 00:08:33.333
Photogrammetry puts him
at about 6 feet.

118
00:08:33.334 --> 00:08:36.437
But other than that. he may
as well have worn the mask.

119
00:08:36.438 --> 00:08:39.714
Which appears to be home made
and is impossible to trace.

120
00:08:40.955 --> 00:08:43.989
- You got anything on the watch?
- Yeah. 300.000 sold

121
00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:46.609
in the past year.
- Can you bring the video up?

122
00:08:50.265 --> 00:08:52.747
<i>Somebody please.
help me!</i>

123
00:08:52.748 --> 00:08:54.920
Behind the scream. can you

124
00:08:54.921 --> 00:08:56.816
isolate that. bring that up.

125
00:08:56.817 --> 00:08:59.645
Yep. Excuse me.

126
00:09:03.748 --> 00:09:05.575
<i>Somebody please help me!</i>

127
00:09:05.576 --> 00:09:07.678
<i>Billy Roland White.
please come to the office.</i>

128
00:09:07.679 --> 00:09:10.092
The murder happened
near a school.

129
00:09:10.093 --> 00:09:12.299
Well. let's make some calls.
Find out what school

130
00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:14.403
has a student named
Billy Roland White.

131
00:09:16.852 --> 00:09:19.747
So the announcement
came from this school.

132
00:09:19.748 --> 00:09:21.747
Takes a certain type
to kill near kids.

133
00:09:21.748 --> 00:09:24.471
Yeah. schools are loud.
chaotic. Even if a kid

134
00:09:24.472 --> 00:09:26.955
does see something.
who's gonna believe him.

135
00:09:37.162 --> 00:09:39.265
You seeing this?
- Yeah.

136
00:09:47.576 --> 00:09:50.369
Oh. you smell that?

137
00:09:56.541 --> 00:09:59.644
Tripod's still
here. but the camera's gone.

138
00:09:59.645 --> 00:10:02.023
Rug's new.

139
00:10:16.058 --> 00:10:18.678
The film was real.

140
00:10:18.679 --> 00:10:21.126
We had the sample processed
as quickly as possible.

141
00:10:21.127 --> 00:10:22.989
but the hydrochloric acid

142
00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:26.540
dissolved all the biological
matter. No traces of DNA.

143
00:10:26.541 --> 00:10:30.023
Ugh. that is grim.
Were there any impurities?

144
00:10:30.024 --> 00:10:33.782
Fillings. pacemaker. anything
at all that could get us an ID?

145
00:10:33.783 --> 00:10:36.920
Found traces of iron.
chromium. and nickel.

146
00:10:36.921 --> 00:10:38.540
but those are most likely
from the watch.

147
00:10:38.541 --> 00:10:41.713
Other than that I wasn't able to
pull anything from the barrel.

148
00:10:41.714 --> 00:10:45.575
Which is why I analyzed a sample
from one of the containers

149
00:10:45.576 --> 00:10:47.195
that was left in the garage.

150
00:10:47.196 --> 00:10:49.851
See. a civilian can't just
order hydrochloric acid

151
00:10:49.852 --> 00:10:52.299
in these quantities.
in case they are

152
00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:53.954
a crazy person in a mask.

153
00:10:53.955 --> 00:10:55.920
Right. This would've had to be
purchased commercially.

154
00:10:55.921 --> 00:10:57.782
And then stolen or sold.

155
00:10:57.783 --> 00:11:00.954
The sample was 37 percent
purity. usually used

156
00:11:00.955 --> 00:11:03.954
in steel mills. So I used
the lot number to track down

157
00:11:03.955 --> 00:11:08.644
the manufacturer. This container
belongs to Atkinson Steel.

158
00:11:08.645 --> 00:11:10.092
I can assure you

159
00:11:10.093 --> 00:11:11.989
that all of our stock
is completely intact.

160
00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:13.920
But if you'd like to learn how
steel is made.

161
00:11:13.921 --> 00:11:16.092
I'd be happy to give you a tour.

162
00:11:16.093 --> 00:11:18.954
No. that's okay. I already
know how steel is made.

163
00:11:18.955 --> 00:11:21.782
I even know how
it degrades over time.

164
00:11:21.783 --> 00:11:25.644
Water and oxygen causing
it to develop iron oxide.

165
00:11:25.645 --> 00:11:29.126
But this lock looks brand new.

166
00:11:29.127 --> 00:11:33.644
- Is that a bad thing?
- No. it's a suspicious thing.

167
00:11:33.645 --> 00:11:38.610
Especially considering
this old lock was smashed.

168
00:11:39.231 --> 00:11:41.023
We have pieces of metal
all over the place.

169
00:11:41.024 --> 00:11:43.816
Well. you also have cameras
all over the place.

170
00:11:43.817 --> 00:11:45.989
Show us some footage of you
replacing that lock.

171
00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:48.023
and we'll get out of your hair.

172
00:11:48.024 --> 00:11:50.851
Last week during the night
shift. I went out for a smoke.

173
00:11:50.852 --> 00:11:54.402
I usually take a couple of laps.
But when I came back.

174
00:11:54.403 --> 00:11:56.126
the lock was already broken.

175
00:11:56.127 --> 00:11:59.920
And 95 litres of
hydrochloric acid was missing.

176
00:11:59.921 --> 00:12:01.747
I couldn't tell that
anything was missing.

177
00:12:01.748 --> 00:12:03.161
You could tell that
the lock was broken.

178
00:12:03.162 --> 00:12:06.368
Please. I can't lose this job.

179
00:12:06.369 --> 00:12:07.644
So you replace the lock.

180
00:12:07.645 --> 00:12:09.264
You make it look like
nothing happened.

181
00:12:09.265 --> 00:12:13.609
We need access
to those cameras. Javier.

182
00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:15.161
I deleted the footage.

183
00:12:15.162 --> 00:12:16.713
That. unfortunately.

184
00:12:16.714 --> 00:12:19.299
is obstructing
a murder investigation.

185
00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.609
Okay. okay. But what if
I know who did it?

186
00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:23.782
He was driving off
as I was coming back

187
00:12:23.783 --> 00:12:26.161
I recognized the car.

188
00:12:26.162 --> 00:12:29.333
Ryan Gray. Creep used to work
here til they sacked him.

189
00:12:29.334 --> 00:12:30.851
Creep?

190
00:12:30.852 --> 00:12:33.609
He set the foreman's car
on fire. The guy's nuts.

191
00:12:35.472 --> 00:12:39.368
I haven't seen
Ryan since Friday.

192
00:12:39.369 --> 00:12:42.299
He borrowed my car.
so I haven't been able to get

193
00:12:42.300 --> 00:12:47.023
to the grocery store.
but he'll be back.

194
00:12:47.024 --> 00:12:48.747
He. he takes care of me.

195
00:12:48.748 --> 00:12:51.402
By um. letting you sleep
on the couch?

196
00:12:51.403 --> 00:12:53.057
Well there's only one bedroom.

197
00:12:53.058 --> 00:12:55.402
and Ryan needs his sleep.

198
00:12:55.403 --> 00:12:58.368
Anyway. he wouldn't want
me blathering--

199
00:12:58.369 --> 00:13:00.126
Mrs. Gray. please.

200
00:13:00.127 --> 00:13:02.920
We're worried your son might
be in some serious trouble.

201
00:13:02.921 --> 00:13:06.609
We just want you to know that
if Ryan is guilty

202
00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:10.023
of what we think he is guilty
of. he could go to jail

203
00:13:10.024 --> 00:13:12.058
for a very long time.

204
00:13:15.369 --> 00:13:20.506
Well. I shouldn't tell you.
but I did find a stack

205
00:13:20.507 --> 00:13:25.057
of one hundred dollar bills
in his dresser last week.

206
00:13:25.058 --> 00:13:26.852
How thick was this stack?

207
00:13:28.438 --> 00:13:33.092
So as thick as a deck
of playing cards.

208
00:13:33.093 --> 00:13:34.714
That's about 40.000.

209
00:13:36.058 --> 00:13:37.920
Uh. is the money
still in the house?

210
00:13:37.921 --> 00:13:39.541
It was gone the next day.

211
00:13:40.541 --> 00:13:45.955
Shirley. could you tell us
if you recognize this balaclava?

212
00:13:46.748 --> 00:13:50.437
Aw. of course.

213
00:13:50.438 --> 00:13:54.472
I
knit this for halloween
when Ryan was a kid.

214
00:13:56.955 --> 00:14:00.714
He used to be such a sweet boy.

215
00:14:25.127 --> 00:14:27.402
Hey.

216
00:14:27.403 --> 00:14:29.713
What're you doing?

217
00:14:41.334 --> 00:14:44.195
We put out a Canada-wide
warrant. Ryan Gray's face

218
00:14:44.196 --> 00:14:47.782
is everywhere. Borders.
airports. rental car agencies.

219
00:14:47.783 --> 00:14:49.885
Still. the guy could be
on a greyhound bus to anywhere

220
00:14:49.886 --> 00:14:52.195
by now. What about the phone
number his mother gave us.

221
00:14:52.196 --> 00:14:54.575
No. it's a dead end.
He must be using a burner.

222
00:14:54.576 --> 00:14:57.954
The money that Ryan's mother
found is bothering me.

223
00:14:57.955 --> 00:15:00.989
It's bothering me
too. If I had 40.000 dollars

224
00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:02.678
I wouldn't be crashing
with my mom.

225
00:15:02.679 --> 00:15:04.333
That money's recent.

226
00:15:04.334 --> 00:15:06.540
Do you think someone could've
hired Ryan to make that film?

227
00:15:06.541 --> 00:15:10.126
And. if it was just a snuff
film. why wouldn't Ryan

228
00:15:10.127 --> 00:15:12.713
choose a more transient victim
who no one might miss.

229
00:15:12.714 --> 00:15:15.713
Our victim had nice
clothes. nice watch.

230
00:15:15.714 --> 00:15:18.886
And a family.
Noticed this. and enhanced it.

231
00:15:20.438 --> 00:15:22.092
Dad.

232
00:15:22.093 --> 00:15:25.679
So. maybe this wasn't random.
Maybe it was a targeted hit.

233
00:15:26.921 --> 00:15:31.990
Well then maybe whoever hired
Ryan also cast the lead role.

234
00:15:39.886 --> 00:15:41.713
Hmmm.
Some good news

235
00:15:41.714 --> 00:15:43.920
over night. They found
Shirley Gray's mini van

236
00:15:43.921 --> 00:15:46.506
at Pearson airport. It's been
there since last Saturday.

237
00:15:46.507 --> 00:15:49.540
That's only good news if Ryan
Gray did not get on a plane.

238
00:15:49.541 --> 00:15:52.126
Well he's not on any flight
manifests. and we're using

239
00:15:52.127 --> 00:15:54.644
facial recognition in case
he's got a fake passport.

240
00:15:54.645 --> 00:15:56.782
I misjudged this guy.
I thought we'd have him by now.

241
00:15:56.783 --> 00:15:59.471
I mean look at him.
he's wearing a damn tea cozy.

242
00:15:59.472 --> 00:16:01.230
Okay. let's say that
this was a targeted hit.

243
00:16:01.231 --> 00:16:04.920
Why make the murder public
in such a horrific way?

244
00:16:04.921 --> 00:16:07.092
Well there's only two people
who know the answer to that.

245
00:16:07.093 --> 00:16:08.816
Ryan Gray and the person
who hired him.

246
00:16:08.817 --> 00:16:10.920
And we still have no idea
who our victim is.

247
00:16:10.921 --> 00:16:13.264
He was thrown in the back
of Shirley Gray's van.

248
00:16:13.265 --> 00:16:15.920
There must be some evidence.
some DNA.

249
00:16:15.921 --> 00:16:20.195
They're still processing
the car. but they also...

250
00:16:20.196 --> 00:16:21.920
sent this over.

251
00:16:21.921 --> 00:16:24.437
The next time I see you parked
in this spot

252
00:16:24.438 --> 00:16:26.885
I will have you towed.
Shefa shop?

253
00:16:26.886 --> 00:16:28.955
It's a store in a strip mall
up in North York.

254
00:16:31.955 --> 00:16:34.747
Hmm. the killer's pretty
far from home.

255
00:16:34.748 --> 00:16:38.092
Maybe he was meeting someone.
Someone with 40k in cash

256
00:16:38.093 --> 00:16:41.920
and a serious grudge.
Oh.

257
00:16:41.921 --> 00:16:44.609
Patience.

258
00:16:47.886 --> 00:16:49.678
Are you planning on
shopping in here?

259
00:16:49.679 --> 00:16:51.230
Uh. ma'am we're the police.

260
00:16:51.231 --> 00:16:53.989
I don't care if you're
the king of Siam.

261
00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:56.402
This is detective Graff.
I'm detective Bateman.

262
00:16:56.403 --> 00:16:59.299
What's your name?
- Esther Severski.

263
00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:02.644
Store owner.
- Well. Ms. Severski.

264
00:17:02.645 --> 00:17:07.368
Do you recall putting this note
on a tan mini van last week?

265
00:17:07.369 --> 00:17:11.989
Thursday. After a week of that
Schmendrick parking in my spot.

266
00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:14.644
I decided to put a note
on the windshield because

267
00:17:14.645 --> 00:17:17.195
he looked very dangerous.

268
00:17:17.196 --> 00:17:20.092
But it worked. because then
on Friday I saw he was parked

269
00:17:20.093 --> 00:17:21.333
behind the furniture shop.

270
00:17:21.334 --> 00:17:23.333
Well. thank you so much
for your time.

271
00:17:27.783 --> 00:17:29.644
So Ryan was parked here
for a whole week.

272
00:17:29.645 --> 00:17:31.609
Yeah. it doesn't sound like
he was meeting the man

273
00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:34.954
who hired him. Sounds like
he was doing surveillance.

274
00:17:34.955 --> 00:17:36.333
Maybe of his victim.

275
00:17:36.334 --> 00:17:38.885
So he parks his car behind
the furniture store

276
00:17:38.886 --> 00:17:40.368
the day of murder.

277
00:17:40.369 --> 00:17:41.989
Closing in on his target?

278
00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:45.299
Officers. Shopping for
a comfortable couch?

279
00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:46.920
Brighten up the break room.

280
00:17:46.921 --> 00:17:49.195
If only we had the budget.
No. we're here to inquire about

281
00:17:49.196 --> 00:17:51.747
a mini van that was parked out
the back of your store

282
00:17:51.748 --> 00:17:54.023
last Friday.
- Friday. I wasn't here.

283
00:17:54.024 --> 00:17:55.299
Who was?

284
00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.299
- New guy. David Barnes.
- Is he here now?

285
00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:01.195
No. It's crazy. but he begged
me for this job.

286
00:18:01.196 --> 00:18:03.057
and then he missed both
his shifts this week.

287
00:18:03.058 --> 00:18:05.402
The last time he was here
he left the store unlocked.

288
00:18:05.403 --> 00:18:09.264
Baruch Hashem nothing was taken.
He's all right. I hope.

289
00:18:09.265 --> 00:18:10.747
Footage from
the furniture store.

290
00:18:10.748 --> 00:18:12.437
Friday at 1 08 P.M.

291
00:18:12.438 --> 00:18:15.678
This employee David Barnes
helping the suspect Ryan Gray

292
00:18:15.679 --> 00:18:18.264
carry a large rug
out the back exit.

293
00:18:18.265 --> 00:18:20.057
David never re enters the store.

294
00:18:20.058 --> 00:18:21.816
So Ryan gets David
to help him move the rug

295
00:18:21.817 --> 00:18:25.057
into the back of the mini van.

296
00:18:25.058 --> 00:18:28.540
pushes him in and
incapacitates him somehow.

297
00:18:28.541 --> 00:18:30.954
Maybe chloroform. maybe drugs.

298
00:18:30.955 --> 00:18:32.920
That is a match for the rug
in the garage.

299
00:18:32.921 --> 00:18:36.092
He helped the guy move the rug
he was rolled in. That's cold.

300
00:18:36.093 --> 00:18:39.333
Pause it.

301
00:18:39.334 --> 00:18:41.264
Zoom in on his wrist.

302
00:18:42.955 --> 00:18:44.747
That's the bracelet
our victim was wearing.

303
00:18:44.748 --> 00:18:47.093
Before it was dissolved
in acid.

304
00:18:48.438 --> 00:18:52.023
I'm sorry. I don't
understand. Is David okay?

305
00:18:52.024 --> 00:18:55.161
Are you aware of anyone who
might've wanted

306
00:18:55.162 --> 00:18:57.023
to harm your husband?

307
00:18:57.024 --> 00:19:01.954
No. I mean. David and I lead
very different lives.

308
00:19:01.955 --> 00:19:04.264
He goes out a lot.
I'm usually with Logan.

309
00:19:04.265 --> 00:19:05.506
or working.

310
00:19:05.507 --> 00:19:07.093
You two back
from the store already?

311
00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:10.264
- Nell. what's going on?
- Uh. dad. can you.

312
00:19:10.265 --> 00:19:12.265
can you take Logan
to the park or something?

313
00:19:17.231 --> 00:19:20.506
Hi. Logan.
My name's Henry.

314
00:19:20.507 --> 00:19:22.955
- Hi Henry.
- Oh.

315
00:19:24.403 --> 00:19:26.126
Have you ever been
to the arctic.

316
00:19:26.127 --> 00:19:27.471
Yep. Have you?

317
00:19:27.472 --> 00:19:29.954
Not yet. My dad's taking me.

318
00:19:29.955 --> 00:19:33.299
Did you know that in Yellowknife
you can see the northern lights

319
00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:35.816
for 240 nights a year?

320
00:19:35.817 --> 00:19:39.057
Yep. And did you know that
astronauts can see

321
00:19:39.058 --> 00:19:40.782
the northern lights from space?

322
00:19:40.783 --> 00:19:43.195
- Woah!
- Woah.

323
00:19:43.196 --> 00:19:44.368
Grab your glove. Logan.

324
00:19:44.369 --> 00:19:46.126
We'll play a little catch
in the park.

325
00:19:46.127 --> 00:19:47.300
Okay.

326
00:19:57.196 --> 00:19:59.816
A left handed glove. I guess
he throws with his right.

327
00:19:59.817 --> 00:20:02.368
Yeah. Logan's right handed.

328
00:20:02.369 --> 00:20:04.989
But he shook my hand
with his left.

329
00:20:06.714 --> 00:20:10.368
Yeah. uh. a few months back
he fell on the playground

330
00:20:10.369 --> 00:20:12.920
and um. hurt his arm.

331
00:20:12.921 --> 00:20:15.713
Sorry. where is David?

332
00:20:15.714 --> 00:20:17.299
What am I gonna tell my son?

333
00:20:17.300 --> 00:20:20.506
What have you been telling
him? Your husband's been missing

334
00:20:20.507 --> 00:20:22.609
for four days
and you haven't reported.

335
00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:27.333
David's been staying in
a hotel for the past few weeks.

336
00:20:27.334 --> 00:20:30.713
I've just told Logan
that he's away working.

337
00:20:30.714 --> 00:20:32.093
We've been having some issues.

338
00:20:33.921 --> 00:20:35.747
What kind of issues?

339
00:20:35.748 --> 00:20:38.540
Just growing
in different directions.

340
00:20:38.541 --> 00:20:40.264
But we're working on it.

341
00:20:40.265 --> 00:20:42.610
No. marriage is complicated.

342
00:20:50.024 --> 00:20:55.230
Oh. guess this backs up the idea
that David liked to party.

343
00:20:55.231 --> 00:20:58.369
Or perhaps he was taking
the split hard.

344
00:21:01.679 --> 00:21:03.782
- Mmm. There's a laptop.
- I see it.

345
00:21:03.783 --> 00:21:05.714
Let's bag it
and get it to Mark.

346
00:21:08.024 --> 00:21:09.747
What's David's kid's name?

347
00:21:09.748 --> 00:21:11.264
Logan?

348
00:21:11.265 --> 00:21:13.540
Well. I'm in.

349
00:21:13.541 --> 00:21:15.092
- Really?
- Yeah.

350
00:21:15.093 --> 00:21:17.333
Well that's not a man with
a lot to hide.

351
00:21:17.334 --> 00:21:21.023
He's got three tabs open
for divorce lawyers.

352
00:21:21.024 --> 00:21:24.161
Looks like he wasn't as into
reconciliation as his wife.

353
00:21:24.162 --> 00:21:26.816
What about that maps tab?

354
00:21:26.817 --> 00:21:30.195
Well that would be the last
address David ever searched.

355
00:21:32.093 --> 00:21:35.506
My niece and Logan
are friends. yeah.

356
00:21:35.507 --> 00:21:37.851
Kids never happened for me. so.

357
00:21:37.852 --> 00:21:40.126
I don't know. I just. I pretty
much piggyback off

358
00:21:40.127 --> 00:21:41.575
my sister's family.

359
00:21:41.576 --> 00:21:44.023
But yeah. David and I ended up
taking Edie and Logan

360
00:21:44.024 --> 00:21:45.299
to a few Jays games last year.

361
00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:47.713
How 'bout them Blue Jays?

362
00:21:47.714 --> 00:21:51.333
Nah. man. Too much heartbreak
for me. I'm a Cubs fan now.

363
00:21:51.334 --> 00:21:53.126
I like the old ball park.

364
00:21:53.127 --> 00:21:57.471
What's going on here? You have
a fight with your planter?

365
00:21:57.472 --> 00:21:59.299
No. that was David.

366
00:21:59.300 --> 00:22:01.920
So it wasn't a friendly visit?

367
00:22:01.921 --> 00:22:03.989
Things have gotten tense.

368
00:22:03.990 --> 00:22:06.506
Truth is. I wasn't a fan
of how he treated Logan.

369
00:22:06.507 --> 00:22:08.851
Treated him how?
What do you mean?

370
00:22:08.852 --> 00:22:11.644
So. a few months back.
we're at the playground.

371
00:22:11.645 --> 00:22:14.402
We're tipping the flask.

372
00:22:14.403 --> 00:22:17.609
And. um. David's really starting
to feel it. I could tell.

373
00:22:17.610 --> 00:22:20.782
Anyway. it's time to go.
and Logan's not listening.

374
00:22:20.783 --> 00:22:22.885
Typical kid stuff. right?

375
00:22:22.886 --> 00:22:26.989
He goes down the slide one more
time. and David goes ballistic.

376
00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:29.747
He grabs his poor kid by the arm
and he throws him to the ground.

377
00:22:29.748 --> 00:22:32.057
He ends up breaking Logan's arm.

378
00:22:32.058 --> 00:22:34.057
David's wife said
that was an accident.

379
00:22:34.058 --> 00:22:35.540
If I got treated
like Nell did.

380
00:22:35.541 --> 00:22:37.057
I'd probably say the same thing.

381
00:22:37.058 --> 00:22:38.885
I'm surprised she even
confronted him about it.

382
00:22:38.886 --> 00:22:40.540
but she must have. because
the next thing I know

383
00:22:40.541 --> 00:22:42.609
he's at my door. drunk.
yelling at me. telling me

384
00:22:42.610 --> 00:22:43.920
that I ruined his life.

385
00:22:43.921 --> 00:22:46.126
- You call the police?
- I threatened to.

386
00:22:46.127 --> 00:22:47.989
Got him to go away.

387
00:22:47.990 --> 00:22:50.506
Nell tells us she and David
are working on things.

388
00:22:50.507 --> 00:22:53.368
but she doesn't tell us that
David broke her kid's arm?

389
00:22:53.369 --> 00:22:55.678
Why would she hide that.

390
00:22:55.679 --> 00:22:58.678
Maybe Nell took care of it
herself. Hired Ryan Gray

391
00:22:58.679 --> 00:23:03.402
to kill David.
and protect her son.

392
00:23:29.507 --> 00:23:34.921
Nell. Why didn't you tell us
that David broke Logan's arm?

393
00:23:35.438 --> 00:23:38.644
What. so you could question
him about it?

394
00:23:38.645 --> 00:23:41.575
I don't want Logan
to relive that.

395
00:23:41.576 --> 00:23:43.057
It took long enough for him
to get comfortable

396
00:23:43.058 --> 00:23:44.437
to tell me the truth.

397
00:23:44.438 --> 00:23:47.540
Or. maybe you didn't want it
to happen again.

398
00:23:47.541 --> 00:23:51.747
You were finally going to leave
your husband. weren't you?

399
00:23:51.748 --> 00:23:55.920
I'm guessing David wasn't
happy about that. you know?

400
00:23:55.921 --> 00:23:58.023
I mean if he broke down
Sebastian's door.

401
00:23:58.024 --> 00:24:00.954
I can't imagine what he would
do to you. to your son.

402
00:24:00.955 --> 00:24:03.575
David had been in a tough
place lately.

403
00:24:03.576 --> 00:24:06.195
He hadn't worked in years.
and I run this successful

404
00:24:06.196 --> 00:24:09.264
skincare company. You understand
what that does to the male ego.

405
00:24:09.265 --> 00:24:12.368
Did anyone else know
about the abuse?

406
00:24:12.369 --> 00:24:17.816
Sebastian knew because
he saw it.

407
00:24:17.817 --> 00:24:20.299
I had a hard enough time
telling my lawyer about it.

408
00:24:20.300 --> 00:24:21.921
Your divorce lawyer?

409
00:24:24.058 --> 00:24:26.023
We were filing
a restraining order.

410
00:24:26.024 --> 00:24:29.057
David was gonna be legally out
of our lives.

411
00:24:29.058 --> 00:24:32.816
I was gonna win sole custody.
I didn't need him dead.

412
00:24:34.990 --> 00:24:36.540
I'll wave attorney
client privilege.

413
00:24:36.541 --> 00:24:38.990
you can ask him yourself.

414
00:24:40.852 --> 00:24:43.713
Look. I had David Barnes
on a skewer. Told him that.

415
00:24:43.714 --> 00:24:45.644
Low key insisted
he sign over custody.

416
00:24:45.645 --> 00:24:47.402
Nell was waving support.
it was a good deal.

417
00:24:47.403 --> 00:24:49.092
She just wanted them
out of their lives.

418
00:24:49.093 --> 00:24:54.437
But he got angry. Said the
courts always favor the mother.

419
00:24:54.438 --> 00:24:56.402
- Is that what you think?
- Wouldn't have mattered.

420
00:24:56.403 --> 00:24:58.402
Nell was financially stable.
and David had a history

421
00:24:58.403 --> 00:24:59.851
of substance abuse
and violence.

422
00:24:59.852 --> 00:25:02.402
- Who else can vouch for that?
- Valid. detective.

423
00:25:02.403 --> 00:25:04.264
Believe women isn't a
recognized legal principle

424
00:25:04.265 --> 00:25:07.161
in any jurisdiction. Nell had
recorded other incidents.

425
00:25:07.162 --> 00:25:10.092
but we needed witnesses
to David's temper.

426
00:25:10.093 --> 00:25:11.989
Nell didn't want her father
getting involved. but I felt--

427
00:25:11.990 --> 00:25:13.747
You brought him in anyway.

428
00:25:13.748 --> 00:25:15.920
Testimony from a grandparent
can win a case.

429
00:25:15.921 --> 00:25:18.299
Did Nell's father
corroborate her accusations?

430
00:25:18.300 --> 00:25:21.299
No. he was in shock.
and he left.

431
00:25:21.300 --> 00:25:22.954
Did Nell know
that you were meeting

432
00:25:22.955 --> 00:25:24.747
with her father recently?

433
00:25:24.748 --> 00:25:27.023
Yeah. She didn't want him
getting invovled.

434
00:25:27.024 --> 00:25:30.575
but I wanted to win the case.

435
00:25:30.576 --> 00:25:34.024
Excuse me. Marcy! Dammit.

436
00:25:35.748 --> 00:25:37.437
Nell was telling the truth.

437
00:25:37.438 --> 00:25:38.989
She was about to get
full custody.

438
00:25:38.990 --> 00:25:41.747
Yeah. but she was lying about
who knew about the abuse.

439
00:25:41.748 --> 00:25:44.368
She knew her lawyer
spoke to her father.

440
00:25:44.369 --> 00:25:47.402
Well. maybe when he saw what
David did to his grandson.

441
00:25:47.403 --> 00:25:50.816
he didn't care so much about
custody. he wanted revenge.

442
00:25:50.817 --> 00:25:56.161
Ah. the ancient guardian.
selfless patriarch.

443
00:25:56.162 --> 00:25:59.023
How'd you react when you found
out it was your son in law

444
00:25:59.024 --> 00:26:02.126
who broke Logan's arm?
You saw the statement.

445
00:26:02.127 --> 00:26:05.816
How he pulled Logan
off the slide.

446
00:26:05.817 --> 00:26:07.885
You know the force it takes
to break bone?

447
00:26:07.886 --> 00:26:11.885
That's enough. Now look.
I spoke with Logan right after

448
00:26:11.886 --> 00:26:15.023
the playground incident.
He said he fell.

449
00:26:15.024 --> 00:26:17.299
Nothing about David pulling him.

450
00:26:17.300 --> 00:26:18.713
But after Nell took him
to the hospital.

451
00:26:18.714 --> 00:26:19.885
he came back with
a different story.

452
00:26:19.886 --> 00:26:21.506
Suddenly it was David's fault.

453
00:26:21.507 --> 00:26:23.816
Maybe he didn't feel
safe saying it

454
00:26:23.817 --> 00:26:26.609
until he had assurance from
his mother that it was okay.

455
00:26:26.610 --> 00:26:28.816
Maybe...

456
00:26:28.817 --> 00:26:31.368
But there's something else.

457
00:26:31.369 --> 00:26:33.368
When Logan was two
he fell out of his high chair

458
00:26:33.369 --> 00:26:37.506
and had to go to emerge.
He was fine. but...

459
00:26:37.507 --> 00:26:41.782
I felt terrible.
because it was me

460
00:26:41.783 --> 00:26:43.644
who forgot to do up
the safety straps.

461
00:26:43.645 --> 00:26:45.195
But in her lawyer's file.

462
00:26:45.196 --> 00:26:47.954
Nell is claiming that David
pushed the high chair over.

463
00:26:47.955 --> 00:26:50.851
So you think that
she's fabricating abuse?

464
00:26:50.852 --> 00:26:52.782
Nell calls David
an unemployed deadbeat.

465
00:26:52.783 --> 00:26:55.954
but I'm their financial advisor.
I was part of the decision

466
00:26:55.955 --> 00:26:58.644
that David assume the role
of stay at home dad.

467
00:26:58.645 --> 00:27:02.575
Why would Nell. or your
daughter. go to such lengths

468
00:27:02.576 --> 00:27:05.300
to separate Logan
from his father?

469
00:27:07.817 --> 00:27:12.576
Nell has been offered a very
good job in Chicago.

470
00:27:13.472 --> 00:27:16.057
And David could stop her
from taking Logan

471
00:27:16.058 --> 00:27:18.057
unless she had full custody.

472
00:27:18.058 --> 00:27:21.540
I love my daughter.

473
00:27:21.541 --> 00:27:23.782
But since she was tiny.
Nell has never let anyone

474
00:27:23.783 --> 00:27:25.782
get in the way
of what she wants.

475
00:27:25.783 --> 00:27:27.575
I can't imagine
you wanted to lose

476
00:27:27.576 --> 00:27:29.057
your grandson to Chicago.

477
00:27:29.058 --> 00:27:31.264
I didn't.

478
00:27:31.265 --> 00:27:34.402
So I went to my lawyer to.
about David fight back.

479
00:27:34.403 --> 00:27:36.195
Did David know you were
planning to help him?

480
00:27:36.196 --> 00:27:38.644
No. I was waiting to hear back
from my lawyer

481
00:27:38.645 --> 00:27:40.195
to see if we had a case.

482
00:27:40.196 --> 00:27:42.264
But it was shakey. because
there was a witness claiming

483
00:27:42.265 --> 00:27:44.713
David broke Logan's arm.
- Sebastian Mercer.

484
00:27:44.714 --> 00:27:46.230
I went to see the man.

485
00:27:46.231 --> 00:27:48.541
But he held strong with his
version of events.

486
00:27:53.058 --> 00:27:54.920
- Sebastian?
- I need to talk to you.

487
00:27:54.921 --> 00:27:56.161
In the middle of the day?

488
00:27:56.162 --> 00:27:58.885
Why haven't you been
answering my calls?

489
00:27:58.886 --> 00:28:01.540
Listen. I. um.
I need to tell you something.

490
00:28:01.541 --> 00:28:04.092
- Is this about David?
